  "refusal_text": "a covered symbol is missing at one of the two revisions and is not on the allowed-introduction list, so the invariance claim cannot be checked: {'hope_commands.py': ['action_ball_live_answer_input_digest', 'action_ball_answer_input_contract', '_ACTION_BALL_ANSWER_INPUT_SCHEMA_VERSION', '_ACTION_BALL_ANSWER_INPUT_PROTOTYPE_COLUMNS', 'action_ball_assert_solver_adapter_binds_these_entry_points', '_ActionBallPoolSolverAdapter.action_ball_bound_entry_points']}",
  "tool": "hope_training/whole_body_tracking/scripts/migrate_action_ball_solver_pin_to_semantic_surface.py",
  "verdict": "REFUSED",
  "what_it_can_and_cannot_certify": "The script certifies a pure re-signing: schema v2 -> v3 with no covered symbol moving except the pin's own declaration half. This round is not that. The escape fixes deliberately changed three covered solve entry points (they now call two new contracts) and added six covered symbols, so the static invariance claim the script checks is false by construction and it says so.",
  "why_it_was_run_anyway": "It is the only tool that certifies a re-signing, so it was run rather than skipped, and its refusal is published rather than worked around. Its allow-lists were NOT edited: widening ALLOWED_MOVED_SYMBOLS to admit _action_ball_refill_pool_many would pre-approve the one symbol that draws the questions, which is the opposite of what the gate is for.",
  "why_the_moved_symbols_did_not_move_an_answer": "The three refused movers are _action_ball_refill_pool_many, _action_ball_frozen_eval_solve and _action_ball_replay_emitted_tasks -- the three covered solve entry points. Each moved because it now calls action_ball_assert_solver_adapter_binds_these_entry_points and action_ball_answer_input_contract before solving. A static digest cannot tell an added refusal from an added computation, which is why the gate refuses. The live-value evidence is what settles it: the tape is produced by running _action_ball_refill_pool_many, and base_question_sha256 came out byte-identical, so the draw did not move. That is a measurement, not an argument."
 },
